#
# Competency (cross-slice compose — the externally-supplied base model artifact): the preference
# gmeow:deltaBaseArtifact leg composes a gmeow:ModelConfigDelta with a served model checkpoint
# minted by whatever slice owns the serving stack (in the worked scene, model-serving's
# gmeow:ModelArtifact) — reused BY REFERENCE, never by a range axiom (Principle 16).
#
# The join is on the CORE seam that reuse actually rides: gmeow:contentDigest. That is not a
# weaker proxy for "is it a gmeow:ModelArtifact" — it is what the leg is FOR. The delta's identity
# is its digest over the whole eleven-leg tuple (AC5), so a base checkpoint that carries no content
# digest cannot make the delta reproducible, whatever it is typed. Naming model-serving's class
# here instead would make this query a semantic dependency edge on a sibling extension (purrdf
# EdgeKind::Query), which Principle 16 forbids; the instance-level typing is demonstrated where the
# tier model allows it, in examples/model-delta-worked.ttl.
#
# Over the model-delta-worked pass scene this returns exactly one row: the delta joined to the
# content-digested base checkpoint its gmeow:deltaBaseArtifact leg names.
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
SELECT ?delta ?baseArtifact WHERE {
    ?delta a gmeow:ModelConfigDelta ;
        gmeow:deltaBaseArtifact ?baseArtifact .
    ?baseArtifact gmeow:contentDigest ?baseDigest .
}
ORDER BY ?delta
